# spec-id-carrier — which git ref namespace this repository uses to hold spec-id
# reservations (spec 0112).
#
# A reservation is a parentless git object pushed to a ref under the namespace
# named here. The guarantee that two sessions never walk away with the same id
# is the remote's create-only compare-and-swap on that ref, so the namespace
# MUST be identical for every contributor — otherwise two contributors writing
# into two different namespaces both succeed and both hold the same id. That is
# why this setting is a tracked, repository-scoped file changed by pull request,
# and not a contributor-local environment variable.
#
# Format: `carrier=<namespace>`. Blank lines and lines whose first non-blank
# character is `#` are ignored; the first `carrier=` line wins.
#
# The value is constrained to a CLOSED PAIR. Anything else — including a near
# miss such as `refs/spec-id/` — makes scripts/reserve-spec-id.sh exit 1 naming
# the offending value, because a third namespace would be written by the push
# and read by neither the allocation union nor
# scripts/check-spec-id-reserved.sh:
#
#   refs/spec-ids/        the default. Invisible in branch and tag listings.
#   refs/tags/spec-id/    the alternative, for a remote that refuses a custom
#                         top-level namespace. Visible in the tag listing.
#
# Org reservations (specs under `specs/org/`, secured with
# `--corpus org --id <ID>`) go to the SIBLING namespace of whichever value is
# set here — `refs/spec-ids-org/` or `refs/tags/spec-id-org/`. Sibling, never a
# child: an `ls-remote` pattern's `*` crosses `/`, so a nested `refs/spec-ids/org/`
# would be returned by a read of `refs/spec-ids/*` and org reservations would
# leak into the upstream allocated set that spec 0112 delta-01 excludes them from.
#
# This entry is `excluded` in .crewrig/core-paths.txt: an adopter whose remote
# refuses the default changes the value once and scripts/sync-from-upstream.sh
# never guards, restores, or aborts on it. The consequence is symmetric and
# permanent — upstream can never update the value afterwards either.
carrier=refs/spec-ids/
